event: warnings
data: ["Official AQI is an index of several pollutants, not a PM2.5 or PM10 concentration.", "Do not read this as Diwali causing the change: AQI often rises through October and November for seasonal reasons, and other weather and emission changes happen at the same time.", "This is official AQI (an index of several pollutants), not a PM2.5 or PM10 concentration.", "Each bulletin covers 16:00 IST on the previous day to 16:00 IST on its date, so the bulletin dated D+1 reports Diwali evening.", "City AQI is CPCB's average over whichever stations reported; the station mix changes daily.", "Percentage changes are withheld: they vary strongly with the baseline window (see baseline_candidates).", "AQI was already rising in the days before Diwali, so the festival level cannot be attributed to Diwali alone."]

